From 221a3fedf377f668cb09f2a9d17e36cd7255ebb6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zirize <zirize@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 00:33:32 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] vncviewer: client-side scaling (Scale, ScaleFilter, F8 menu)

Scale=Off|Fit|Stretch|Integer scales the remote framebuffer to the
window with XRender; ScaleFilter=Nearest|Linear|IntegerPlus picks the
filter for Fit and Stretch. IntegerPlus scales by the largest integer
with nearest into an intermediate surface, then fills the rest with
bilinear. While scaling, RemoteResize is suspended.

The F8 menu gets a "Display mode" radio submenu that picks how the
session follows the window: resize the remote session, no resize
(scrollbars), or scale locally to fit, stretch or by an integer; and
a "Scale filter" submenu. Changes last for the session.

Scale=Off (the default) behaves exactly like stock. X11 only.
